main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ same-named function hides the struct type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
does not uniquely resolve
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.scope.hiding]/2: a function hides a same-named class/struct in
ordinary (value) lookup, so `box()` calls the function rather than being
ambiguous with the type's constructor.  Regression test for the "does not
uniquely resolve" bug on the C-library struct-tag/function pattern (glibc
`struct mallinfo`/`mallinfo()` in memory_info.cpp).
